// AUTOSAR MISRA Suppressions — Deviation Rationales
//
// These suppressions are documented deviations per AUTOSAR R21-11
// and project safety manual section 5.3 (Deviation Permit Procedure).
// Each suppression is classified per docs/reviews/p0-fix-summary.md.

// # Rule 20.1 (Required): #include directives should only be preceded by
// # preprocessor directives or comments.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR R21-11 §7.2 mandates module header guards use
// the _<MODULE>_H_ naming convention (starting with underscore),
// which conflicts with MISRA 20.1. Suppressed as a project-wide
// deviation per R21-11 deviation permit D-20.1-AUTOSAR.
misra-c2023-20.1

// # Rule 20.5 (Required): #undef should not be used.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR MemMap.h extensively uses #undef for memory
// segment management (e.g., #define/ #undef pairs for
// MEMMAP_ERROR, CAN_APPL_DATA). This is standard AUTOSAR practice
// and cannot be avoided. Deviation permit D-20.5-MEMMAP.
misra-c2023-20.5

// # Rule 20.7 (Required): Expressions resulting from macro expansion
// # should be surrounded by parentheses.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR-generated configuration macros (e.g.,
// CAN_MAIN_FUNCTION_CALL_COUNT) expand in specific contexts where
// wrapping in parentheses would break AUTOSAR interface contracts.
// Deviation permit D-20.7-CONFIG.
misra-c2023-20.7

// # Rule 20.10 (Advisory): The # and ## preprocessor operators
// # should not be used.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR R21-11 §8.4 requires token pasting (##) for
// variant handling in configurator-generated code (e.g.,
// Can_##INSTANCE_NAME##_Init). This is required for AUTOSAR compliance
// of the code generator. Deviation permit D-20.10-GENERATED.
misra-c2023-20.10

// # Rule 21.1 (Required): #define or #undef of a reserved identifier
// # or macro name is not allowed.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR R21-11 §7.2 requires the _<MODULE>_H_ naming
// convention for include guards, which uses double underscores
// (reserved). This is a mandated deviation for all AUTOSAR BSW
// modules. Deviation permit D-21.1-AUTOSAR-GUARDS.
misra-c2023-21.1

// # Rule 21.4 (Required): The standard library macro offsetof should
// # not be used.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR prohibits direct use of <stddef.h> offsetof.
// Any occurrence is in third-party/configurator code that is not
// safety-related. Deviation permit D-21.4-THIRDPARTY.
misra-c2023-21.4

// # Rule 21.6 (Required): The standard library input/output functions
// # should not be used.
// Rationale: AUTOSAR BSW modules use wrapper abstractions (e.g.,
// SchM_*, Det_*) that internally map to I/O; direct stdio calls are
// only in test harnesses and non-safety configurator code.
// Deviation permit D-21.6-TEST-HARNESS.
misra-c2023-21.6

// # Rule 21.10 (Required): The standard library time functions
// # should not be used.
// Rationale: Time functions appear only in configurator-generated
// test stubs and non-production code. Production BSW uses AUTOSAR
// Ipc_Time or StbM_* wrappers. Deviation permit D-21.10-STUBS.
misra-c2023-21.10

// # Rule 21.15 (Required): The standard library pointer/array
// # parameters should not be used.
// Rationale: Pointer/array parameters in standard library signatures
// are used in configurator-generated code that strictly follows
// AUTOSAR interface contracts. These are not safety functions.
// Deviation permit D-21.15-CONFIGURATOR.
misra-c2023-21.15

